Backport of upstream commits e154c1a811021ab0bd6e6f9595c2b3c6518aaea3
("Support build against latest version of libtorrent") and
f278af6cc6c7147a34a07611160a469931541f88 ("Allow to use std::string_view
to construct Path"), both merged to qBittorrent's master after the
release-5.2.4 tag was cut, plus one additional fix of our own (see below).

net-libs/libtorrent-rasterbar-2.1.x reworked lt::storage_params: the
``mapped_files`` optional pointer is gone (replaced by a mandatory
``renamed_files`` reference), and ``path``/``part_file_dir`` changed
from ``std::string`` to ``lt::string_view``. qBittorrent 5.2.4 still
unconditionally used the old members, so it fails to build against
2.1.x with:

  error: 'const struct libtorrent::storage_params' has no member named 'mapped_files'
  error: no matching function for call to 'Path::Path(<brace-enclosed initializer list>)'

Upstream's own fix guards the new field behind
``LIBTORRENT_VERSION_NUM >= 20100`` (i.e. libtorrent >= 2.1.0) and gives
Path a std::string_view constructor to accept storage_params::path
directly, so this applies cleanly to any libtorrent 2.0.x install too
(not just 2.1.x) -- only the trimmed-down parts actually needed for
this ebuild's RDEPEND floor (>=net-libs/libtorrent-rasterbar-2.0.10)
are carried over here.

Our own addition on top of upstream's fix: customstorage.h didn't
previously need LIBTORRENT_VERSION_NUM itself (only customstorage.cpp
did, which pulls it in transitively through other headers included
*before* customstorage.h's own guard is reached). Since
customstorage.h is the very first #include in customstorage.cpp, its
own "#if LIBTORRENT_VERSION_NUM >= 20100" guard for the new
renamedFiles member was being evaluated before the macro was defined
anywhere in the translation unit -- silently taking the false branch
and omitting the member, while the *same* guard in customstorage.cpp's
new_torrent() (reached later, after other includes had pulled in
version.hpp transitively) evaluated true. That mismatch produced a
second, unrelated-looking error:

  error: no match for 'operator=' (operand types are 'CustomDiskIOThread::StorageData' and '<brace-enclosed initializer list>')

Explicitly including <libtorrent/version.hpp> at the top of
customstorage.h (as customstorage.cpp's own transitive includes
happened to, by luck, before) makes the guard evaluate consistently
throughout the whole translation unit.

--- a/src/base/path.h
+++ b/src/base/path.h
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@
     Path() = default;

     explicit Path(const QString &pathStr);
-    explicit Path(const std::string &pathStr);
+    explicit Path(std::string_view pathStr);

     bool isValid() const;
     bool isEmpty() const;
--- a/src/base/path.cpp
+++ b/src/base/path.cpp
@@ -72,8 +72,8 @@
 {
 }

-Path::Path(const std::string &pathStr)
-    : Path(QString::fromStdString(pathStr))
+Path::Path(const std::string_view pathStr)
+    : Path(QString::fromUtf8(pathStr.data(), pathStr.size()))
 {
 }

--- a/src/base/bittorrent/customstorage.h
+++ b/src/base/bittorrent/customstorage.h
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@

 #pragma once

+#include <libtorrent/version.hpp>
 #include <libtorrent/aux_/vector.hpp>
 #include <libtorrent/fwd.hpp>

@@ -98,6 +99,9 @@
     {
         Path savePath;
         lt::file_storage files;
+#if LIBTORRENT_VERSION_NUM >= 20100
+        lt::renamed_files renamedFiles;
+#endif
         lt::aux::vector<lt::download_priority_t, lt::file_index_t> filePriorities;
     };
     QHash<lt::storage_index_t, StorageData> m_storageData;
--- a/src/base/bittorrent/customstorage.cpp
+++ b/src/base/bittorrent/customstorage.cpp
@@ -65,12 +65,16 @@
 {
     lt::storage_holder storageHolder = m_nativeDiskIO->new_torrent(storageParams, torrent);

-    const Path savePath {storageParams.path};
     m_storageData[storageHolder] =
     {
-        savePath,
-        storageParams.mapped_files ? *storageParams.mapped_files : storageParams.files,
-        storageParams.priorities
+        .savePath = Path(storageParams.path),
+#if LIBTORRENT_VERSION_NUM >= 20100
+        .files = storageParams.files,
+        .renamedFiles = storageParams.renamed_files,
+#else
+        .files = storageParams.mapped_files ? *storageParams.mapped_files : storageParams.files,
+#endif
+        .filePriorities = storageParams.priorities
     };

     return storageHolder;
